","type":"text"},{"text":"no element before ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" satisfies the ","type":"text"},{"code":"belongsInSecondPartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"predicate and every element at or after ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" satisfies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"belongsInSecondPartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This operation isn’t guaranteed to be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stable, so the relative ordering of elements within the partitions might","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the following example, an array of numbers is partitioned by a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"predicate that matches elements greater than 30."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var numbers = [30, 40, 20, 30, 30, 60, 10]","let p = numbers.partition(by: { $0 > 30 })","\/\/ p == 5","\/\/ numbers == [30, 10, 20, 30, 30, 60, 40]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"numbers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" array is now arranged in two partitions. The first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"partition, "},{"code":"numbers[..<p]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", is made up of the elements that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are not greater than 30. The second partition, "},{"code":"numbers[p...]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is made up of the elements that "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"are","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" greater than 30."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let first = numbers[..<p]","\/\/ first == [30, 10, 20, 30, 30]","let second = numbers[p...]","\/\/ second == [60, 40]"],"type":"codeListing